# DURABLE REPRO — a `Callable`-typed `&`-PARAMETER ICEs the compiler.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg): `gg check` reports "OK: no semantic
# errors", then `gg build` PANICS:
#
#   GIR validation errors:
#     function @with_it, bb0: call to undefined function @cb
#   thread 'gg-main' panicked at src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:1737:13:
#   GIR module failed validation (1 errors)
#
# So the indirect-call lowering does not recognise `cb` as a CALLABLE LOCAL when
# it arrives as a `Callable[..] &` parameter — it lowers `cb(&v)` as a direct
# call to a function literally named `cb`, which does not exist. An accepted
# program that crashes the compiler is a defect regardless of what the language
# eventually decides about this shape.
#
# ⚠ DISTINCT FROM THE THREE FILED `Callable` SIBLINGS, and the distinguishing
# axis is the SIGIL ON THE PARAMETER, not the argument:
#   A1  `sound_callable_amp_param_indirect_call.gg`  — Callable LOCAL bound to
#       an `&`-param function; `&`-ARG is a whole local        -> SEGFAULT
#   A2  `security/sound_callable_amp_param_projection.gg`      -> SEGFAULT
#       — Callable arrives as a bare PARAM; `&`-ARG is `&c.fd`
#   THIS — the Callable parameter is itself `&`-SIGILLED
#       (`Callable[int(&int)] &cb`)                            -> ICE
# The first two reach the backend and crash at RUNTIME; this one never gets
# there. Do not assume a fix for the segfault family covers this cell.
#
# INTENDED: one of two, and the round that closes this must pick.
#   (a) The shape is meaningful — a `&`-param Callable is an ordinary
#       write-through parameter — so `cb(&v)` lowers as an INDIRECT call and
#       the program prints 11 then 11.
#   (b) A `Callable` may not take the `&` sigil at all (it is a single-owner
#       carve-out type and is simply BORROWED at a call, per AGENTS.md's
#       "Ownership at Consuming Positions"), in which case the reference-grade
#       answer is a CHECK-TIME rejection.
# Either way the ICE is wrong: `gg check` must not pass a program the lowering
# then panics on (Core #10, lower-or-reject).
#
# ⚠ This fixture asserts reading (a). If the round rules (b), REPLACE the
# assertion with the reject rather than deleting the fixture — the ICE is the
# defect under both readings.
#
# ORACLE (ggdef): OUT OF SUBSET — ggdef does not reify a named function into a
# `Callable` value ("unresolved local"), the same gap recorded for A2.
#
# The seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so no const-fold can elide the call.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High).

int seed():
    return 10

int bumpret(int &n):
    n = n + 1
    return n

int with_it(Callable[int(&int)] &cb, int &v):
    return cb(&v)

void main():
    int x = seed()
    Callable[int(&int)] f = bumpret
    print(with_it(&f, &x))
    print(x)
